+#ifdef CHIMERA_VSCHED
+// chimera: here one guest thread runs at a time, in turns (patch 0003). A
+// thread that lets a spin lock go and takes it again within its own turn -
+// a loop that polls something under the lock - leaves a thread waiting for
+// that lock finding it taken at every one of its turns, for good. On the
+// console the two run on different hardware threads, and the waiter gets
+// the lock in between. So while a thread waits for a spin lock, a thread
+// that lets one go gives its turn away at once, and the waiter takes the
+// lock before the other can run again (chimera#387: Dead or Alive 4's sound
+// waited for a lock a job thread kept taking in such a loop, and the game
+// stopped).
+static uint32_t chimera_spin_lock_waiters = 0;
+#endif
